---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Lauren Becherer Pottery · Brett Boggs"
  description="Handmade ceramics, photographed all the way around."
>
  <article>
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Websites · 2026</p>
      <h1>Lauren Becherer Pottery</h1>
      <p class="lede">Handmade ceramics, photographed all the way around.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- The point of this page is the build itself, so the way in comes first. -->
    <a class="launch" href="https://laurenbechererpottery.com">
      <span class="launch-go">Open the site <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
      <span class="launch-meta">Live · work, shop, journal, commissions, client pages</span>
    </a>

    <a class="shot" href="https://laurenbechererpottery.com" aria-label="Open laurenbechererpottery.com">
      <img
        src="/peek/lauren-becherer-pottery-lg.webp"
        alt="The home page of laurenbechererpottery.com, a celadon cup beside the line No two are alike."
        width="1440"
        height="960"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <span class="shot-chip">laurenbechererpottery.com</span>
    </a>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Lauren throws and hand-builds in small batches, and glazes in small batches too, which
        means no two pieces come out the same. One photograph of a pot flattens exactly the thing
        that makes it worth buying. So the site is built around turning the piece instead.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every piece is shot on a turntable and served as a spin you can drag. Thirteen so far.
        Every frame is a real photograph, shot in raw and focus stacked, and the import refuses
        anything else. One early set came back with thirty-four interpolated in-between frames and
        the build stops rather than publish them. A steppy honest turn beats a smooth fake one.
      </p>
      <p>
        She runs it without me. There is a studio login on the site: she signs in with one click,
        edits the page she happens to be looking at, and the site rebuilds itself in about a
        minute. Pieces marked for sale get a Stripe button. Commission requests come in through a
        form, and each commission gets a private progress page reached by a code, so a client can
        watch their piece without anybody else finding it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Astro, static, hosted on GitHub Pages. The domain is the only line item.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a class="back-link" href="/work/websites/">&larr; All websites</a>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .launch {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .launch-go {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 60, 'SOFT' 50, 'WONK' 0;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    color: var(--sienna);
  }
  .launch-go span {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: translate 0.4s var(--ease-warm);
  }
  .launch:hover .launch-go span,
  .launch:focus-visible .launch-go span {
    translate: 0.35rem 0;
  }
  .launch-meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  /* The screenshot is a second, larger target for the same link. */
  .shot {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    line-height: 0;
  }
  .shot img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    transition: scale 0.7s var(--ease-warm);
  }
  .shot:hover img,
  .shot:focus-visible img {
    scale: 1.02;
  }
  .shot-chip {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-right: 2px solid var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .prose {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
  }
  .note {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .launch-go span,
    .shot img {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
